  "evidence": "TEXT_D: +£540m yearly for the NHS (+£200m for frontline staff); restore free eye/dental checks; freeze prescription charges; stronger carers’ support and fairer long‑term care; end rough sleeping by 2000; build more affordable homes and bring empty homes back into use; universal early‑years education for 3–4‑year‑olds; cut primary classes to ≤30; literacy drive and better discipline with transparent results; minimum wage (regionally varied); raise personal allowance and introduce a 50% rate over £100k; Human Rights Commission, equal age of consent, repeal Section 28, tackle racism, and civil rights for disabled; insulate 2m lowest‑income homes; CO2 −30% in 15 years; shift long‑term unemployment benefits into “working benefits” and cut poverty traps; 3,000 more police with a focus on prevention and restorative justice. TEXT_F: Keep Britain the lowest‑tax major economy (target 20p basic rate; top rate capped at 40p); move to a balanced budget; reject the Social Chapter and a national minimum wage; nationwide Project Work with obligations under JSA; rigorous testing, intervention in failing schools, and more grammar/specialist schools; more police, CCTV, mandatory minimum sentences for persistent burglars and hard‑drug dealers; sovereignty-first stance in Europe and opposition to devolution; NHS real‑terms increases, performance publication, and PFI modernisation.",
